175	<section id="problem">
176	  <h2>The problem</h2>
177	  <p class="title">Agents write code fast. Trusting what they wrote is the slow part.</p>
178	  <div class="grid">
179	    <div class="panel bad"><h3>The report isn't the work</h3><p>An agent can say it finished work that its commits don't hold. The gap shows up in the diff, if anyone reads it.</p></div>
180	    <div class="panel bad"><h3>Rules in a prompt drift</h3><p>A prompt can say "keep the tests," but nothing measures whether the agent listened. So there's no way to tell if a stricter rule helps or only costs more.</p></div>
181	    <div class="panel bad"><h3>The agent holds your keys</h3><p>An agent that can push and merge has your credentials in its run. And a run that has seen a credential can't be trusted again.</p></div>
182	    <div class="panel bad"><h3>Sessions don't add up</h3><p>Five agents in five terminals is five things to watch, and nothing says which one is waiting.</p></div>
