186	<section>
187	  <h2>The solution</h2>
188	  <p class="title">Treat each request as a job, and keep every decision that matters with you.</p>
189	  <div class="grid">
190	    <div class="panel ok"><h3>One board for every job</h3><p>Each request becomes a job with its own worktree and sandbox VM. The Jobs page shows them all, with the ones waiting on you first.</p></div>
191	    <div class="panel ok"><h3>You judge artifacts, not claims</h3><p>Every stage leaves something you can check, such as a plan, a test result, or a diff. A comment on one goes to the agent as its next brief.</p></div>
192	    <div class="panel ok"><h3>Rules you can measure</h3><p>Every rule is a hook decision with a level: told, checked, or enforced. Run an eval to see what a stricter level does before you commit to it.</p></div>
193	    <div class="panel ok"><h3>Keys stay out of the sandbox</h3><p>Agents run in sandbox VMs that never see a credential. Pushes and pull requests happen on the host, and a tamper-evident log records every decision.</p></div>
194	  </div>
